      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SIYAASI (1) continues to impress deep into his maiden prep. Raced handy and battled on well under 61.5kgs last start over 1350m at Griffith, clocking in second. Has a win and four placings from five starts on wet tracks. Sure to play a key role again. ROSARY SISTER (4) stepped up to 1400m for the first time and recorded a tidy maiden win at Nowra last time out. Progressing in good style and looks ready to take on this better field. NOIR VITESSE (2) returned from a six-month spell with a modest effort over 1300m at Corowa recently. Not sure he is at his best on tracks with give but his best ratings put him right in contention. The speedy WESTERN LIGHTS (5) knocked up after leading for home over 1200m at Cootamundra last start. Placed at three of five heavy track runs so the surface condition brings her into the conversation. ICONIC ROSE (6) battled on well at the end of 1200m last time so today's trip should suit.",
